SUMMARY:Deadline: MIT Museum: BRAIN Programmatic Open Call (public programs
 )
DESCRIPTION:Companion call to the BRAIN Digital Content Open Call: the MIT 
 Museum seeks public programs exploring humanity's relationship with the BR
 AIN\, its thematic focus from April to September 2027 spanning cognition\,
  neurotechnology\, brain-computer interfaces\, mental health and the bound
 aries of ability.\n\nOrganisation: MIT Museum\nLocation: Cambridge\, Massa
 chusetts\, US (programs take place at the MIT Museum in Kendall Square)\nA
 ward: Up to USD 1\,000 total per selected program\, covering all costs inc
 luding speaker and performer fees\, travel\, materials and equipment renta
 l\; proposals using external funding or smaller budgets welcome. The Museu
 m sets ticket prices and keeps ticket revenue. No application fee.\nDurati
 on: BRAIN thematic focus runs April - September 2027\; accepted programs f
 inalized by 15 December 2026\n\nMore: https://mitmuseum.mit.edu/brain-prog
 rammatic-open-call?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referr
 al
